{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel","id":232420,"title":"GenCon panel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T22:00:21-07:00","id":232420,"title":"GenCon panel","content":"For anyone who wants to bring us up to speed on Saturday's GenCon panel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:19:58-07:00","id":232892,"title":"","content":"From the Con:<br /> <br /> - Trinity Continuum core is modern day; &quot;the world outside your window.&quot; Despite that, there are numerous differences - the Continuum is a more optimistic place to live, and little things like more money in the space program, more environmentalism. Heroes can make a difference, and more importantly, they have.<br /> - There's a &quot;secret history of the world&quot; and the Continuum is plagued by scientific anomalies and causality issues.<br /> - One writer's biggest inspirations were the TV shows Continuum and Fringe.<br /> - Aeon's developer is John Snead. He's looking at making the game more &quot;metaplot agnostic&quot; - setting the game around the latter third of the metaplot, but making it clear that the future of the game may not hold the previous one's in store.<br /> - Important distinction - &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;, not Trinity Universe. The Continuum has a unique relationship with quantum mechanics and time travel, inherent in the way dramatic editing works within the setting. It adds an extra weight to Aberrant and Trinity's assertion that, &quot;no, the future needn't go this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> - The game uses the same base system as Scion, a far more action-oriented version of the Attribute + Ability classic system. You'll see a familiar-looking character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:47:52-07:00","id":232916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=232892#post232892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Important distinction - &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;, not Trinity Universe. The Continuum has a unique relationship with quantum mechanics and time travel, inherent in the way dramatic editing works within the setting. It adds an extra weight to Aberrant and Trinity's assertion that, &quot;no, the future needn't go this way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I've ever been interested in the Trinity Continuum instead of just curious as to what the hell it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:52:49-07:00","id":232920,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall<br /> <br /> Thanks for posting that, just what I was looking for (aside from info on the system doc, of course!). Any chance a post can be made to the main website so this info can more easily be found?<br /> <br /> Thanks again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:42:39-07:00","id":233196,"title":"","content":"There was a Trinity Continuum sample document at the Onyx Path booth after the GenCon panel. I went and read through it the next day. Unfortunately it didn't have any system information, but it did have some great setting content.<br /> <br /> The document was broken into two parts: IC fluff documents from all throughout time that gave little interesting pieces of the setting (some of which seemed like adventure setups), and a partial list of important modern groups that the players can interact with/be part of. The IC setting content was pretty entertaining. I especially liked a really well characterized missive from Houdini to the Aeon Society, which had the most perfect line in the entire document.<br /> <br /> IIRC, the groups chapter had four groups in it:<br /> - The Aeon Foundation (?) - A branch of the Aeon Society that does their operations. The coolest thing I remember from this group is their organization: they have set groups of normal people, and then people with powers act as floating consultants for the organization.<br /> - The second group I don't remember the name of, but they were a group that fought against people that hunted people. The central theme of this group seemed to be that 1) the events of the most dangerous game actually happened, and 2) that they weren't an isolated occurrence but were the result of a secret society that hunted people for fun.<br /> - Again, I don't remember the name of the third group, but they seemed to be based on a certain kind of transhumanist thinker. They are fairly libertarian, sometimes a little morally grey, but strongly against existential risk. Because of this, they fight strongly against nuclear proliferation, self-replicating nanobots, etc.<br /> - A Caribbean/Central American group (leaving them unnamed because their name is changing before release). This is a group of freedom fighters whose goal is to take down dictatorships across the world. I really liked this group a lot. They were depicted in a very positive light, and it was pretty clear that although their methods were morally ambiguous, their goals were good.<br /> <br /> There was a feeling with all of these groups that any could be posed as the heroes or villains of a story. There were also a number of references to a mysterious group called the Lightkeepers either helping out or fighting against various groups. We asked Ian afterward if he could tell us any more about them, and the answer was, &quot;No. They're really awesome, though.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We also got a bit of clarification about rules. As mentioned, characters should be transferable across all systems and still be effective thanks to the environmental dice, so you should be able to, say, play a Scion in your Aberrant game (the example given was Thor). There are also not going to be any more mega stats in Aberrant, and I believe no Legend points in Scion.<br /> <br /> My memory is not great, so if anyone read the document and wants to make an addition or correction, I'd be grateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3720-kumarei","user":"kumarei","date":".  Edit: Correcting Lightbringers to Lightkeepers 08-18-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3720-kumarei","name":"kumarei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:56:08-07:00","id":233204,"title":"","content":"As a draft, literally everything in it is subject to change.<br /> <br /> The other group mentioned is the &quot;Lightkeepers,&quot; not Lightbringers.<br /> <br /> Thor in Aberrant probably wouldn't work very well, to be honest, but if you're willing to do the work, you could do it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, mostly accurate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:58:42-07:00","id":233207,"title":"","content":"Oof, feel like kind of a derp for that Lightkeepers mixup. Too much Song of Ice and Fire on the brain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3720-kumarei","name":"kumarei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:09:40-07:00","id":233324,"title":"","content":"Ian, was the panel recorded, and if so, will it be posted? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:09:48-07:00","id":233548,"title":"","content":"No more mega-attributes in Aberrant?<br /> <br /> That is... I'm not sure if I like that, unless their functionality in the setting and game are being preserved in some other form.<br /> <br /> That would otherwise be a 'do not buy' warning for me on Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:18:33-07:00","id":233554,"title":"","content":"I do not think that they would take away the chance for super-strength. I mean, it is a staple of both comics (that Aberrant took a lot from) and Scion (Hercules, anyone?) so I sincerely doubt that the devs would take that away. It is, more than likely, going to be there in a different form. I have faith in the designers to give us this.<br /> It also applies to Intelligence and Perception and what have you. They would not take these away. I think that they will just be present by a different mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:33:51-07:00","id":233569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233554#post233554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that they would take away the chance for super-strength. I mean, it is a staple of both comics (that Aberrant took a lot from) and Scion (Hercules, anyone?) so I sincerely doubt that the devs would take that away. It is, more than likely, going to be there in a different form. I have faith in the designers to give us this.<br /> It also applies to Intelligence and Perception and what have you. They would not take these away. I think that they will just be present by a different mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do hope so. Most of my favorite characters that I've made in Aberant in the past are defined more by their Mega-Attributes than their Powers. Super intelligence, or charisma, or strength, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:33:00-07:00","id":233625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233548#post233548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is... I'm not sure if I like that, unless their functionality in the setting and game are being preserved in some other form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give us <i>some </i>credit.<br /> <br /> We've just gotten rid of <i>specifically </i>Mega-Attributes, same way Scion got rid of Epic Attributes. We've just got different ways to model the fact that you can lift a VW Beetle over your head and shotput it over a skyscraper, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:39:13-07:00","id":233629,"title":"","content":"See? SEE?<br /> BTW, I will always buy Aeoniverse things. This has always been my favorite line. And I run a Scion game that my players love the hell out of so I have no choice BUT to buy that line, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:58:53-07:00","id":233659,"title":"","content":"Environmental dice? Do we know what those are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/140-samcwic","name":"samcwic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:44:37-07:00","id":233715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233625#post233625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give us <i>some </i>credit.<br /> <br /> We've just gotten rid of <i>specifically </i>Mega-Attributes, same way Scion got rid of Epic Attributes. We've just got different ways to model the fact that you can lift a VW Beetle over your head and shotput it over a skyscraper, that's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the way you put that. Thanks, Neall!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T00:08:13-07:00","id":233920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233625#post233625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give us <i>some </i>credit.<br /> <br /> We've just gotten rid of <i>specifically </i>Mega-Attributes, same way Scion got rid of Epic Attributes. We've just got different ways to model the fact that you can lift a VW Beetle over your head and shotput it over a skyscraper, that's all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As long as I can tear Jormungandr out of the earth and use it as a whip we're golden <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T00:40:32-07:00","id":233947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>samcwic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233659#post233659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Environmental dice? Do we know what those are?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the parallel Scion thread is any indication, Environmental Dice are ones that allow you scale up your power based on being in a suitable environment: in Scion, that means something along the lines of (paraphrasing) places that resonate with your Legend. In the Trinity Continuum, I suspect that it would be something along the lines of \u201cambient Telluric energy\u201d: e.g., put a super-strong Adventure-era Stalwart (capable of bench-pressng a pickup truck) in the Quantum fields that Aberrant-era Novas deal with every day, and he\u2019ll be able to lift skyscrapers and the like. or simething like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T03:54:30-07:00","id":234031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=232892#post232892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes can make a difference, and more importantly, they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;SHUT UP AND TAKE MY MONEY!&quot;<br /> <br /> The ability to make a difference has always been a selling point for me with regards to the Trinity Universe. This will be no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:19:36-07:00","id":234058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the parallel Scion thread is any indication, Environmental Dice are ones that allow you scale up your power based on being in a suitable environment </div> </div> </div>Not just scale up. <br /> <br /> Scale down, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:24:30-07:00","id":234060,"title":"","content":"OTOH, it sounds likely that they\u2019ve chosen to resolve the \u201ctalents\u201d debate on the side of time travel and manipulation of QM\u2019s Uncertainty Principle. If so, I\u2019m going to miss the \u201cheroic baselines\u201d \u2014 though I haven\u2019t <i>completely</i> given up hope yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T05:38:30-07:00","id":234089,"title":"","content":"It's really the von Neumann-Wigner interpretation - sapient but especially sentient life collapses the waveform - but yeah. Talents resolve the outcome of events in the area most favorable to themselves, regardless of improbability. <br /> <br /> It's worth noting that that entire text of Adventure! says they can do this, except the dramatic editing chapter which says that it's all out of character. <br /> <br /> Two caveats:<br /> 1) There's no such thing as baseline heroes, since <i>anyone can do this</i>, but Inspiration is a heroic reflection of unconsciously perceiving the Continuum;<br /> 2) If it bothers you, Talent powers can be segregated into &quot;this is a function of exceptional heroism&quot; and &quot;this is probability manipulation&quot;. I've got a sidebar earmarked for this in the ST chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:36:41-07:00","id":234134,"title":"","content":"That addresses my concerns, especially the \u201canyone can do this\u201d bit. That is, there <i>are</i> \u201cbaseline heroes\u201d; but the \u201cbaseline\u201d in TC is different from the \u201cbaseline\u201d in the real world: you don\u2019t need to be \u201cborn special\u201d or transformed in some way in order to partake in the setting\u2019s heroic conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:07:53-07:00","id":234155,"title":"","content":"Okay that not only blew my concerns out of the water, it caught them in a net, dragged them to land, and strangled them to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:11:33-07:00","id":234195,"title":"","content":"THIS IS GONNA BE AWESOME","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:02:15-07:00","id":234256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234195#post234195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THIS IS GONNA BE AWESOME</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep - despite my lingering reservations this is looking more and more promising, not to mention just plain fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:20:24-07:00","id":234365,"title":"","content":"I was sold when I was told you could use Scion. I\u00b4m going to be making a setting with Children of the Gods, and superheroes in one setting. I is happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:33:45-07:00","id":234659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233625#post233625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give us <i>some </i>credit.<br /> <br /> We've just gotten rid of <i>specifically </i>Mega-Attributes, same way Scion got rid of Epic Attributes. We've just got different ways to model the fact that you can lift a VW Beetle over your head and shotput it over a skyscraper, that's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me one concern - That since the Mega/Epic Attributes are going away, will you still be able to give your ability to think faster than a normal human or be coolly calm &amp; collected in the face of beyond normal circumstances still be granular (i.e. has levels 1-5 like other traits, in other word, a Power) or will they be flat abilities that give X bonus or does this one thing like a talent or birthright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3108-malckuss","name":"Malckuss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:17:00-07:00","id":234707,"title":"","content":"Haven't quite decided on that yet. Things like Intelligence are still rated Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:16:32-07:00","id":234755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=232892#post232892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Con:<br /> <br /> - Trinity Continuum core is modern day; &quot;the world outside your window.&quot; Despite that, there are numerous differences - the Continuum is a more optimistic place to live, and little things like more money in the space program, more environmentalism. Heroes can make a difference, and more importantly, they have.<br /> - There's a &quot;secret history of the world&quot; and the Continuum is plagued by scientific anomalies and causality issues.<br /> - One writer's biggest inspirations were the TV shows Continuum and Fringe.<br /> - Aeon's developer is John Snead. He's looking at making the game more &quot;metaplot agnostic&quot; - setting the game around the latter third of the metaplot, but making it clear that the future of the game may not hold the previous one's in store.<br /> - Important distinction - &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;, not Trinity Universe. The Continuum has a unique relationship with quantum mechanics and time travel, inherent in the way dramatic editing works within the setting. It adds an extra weight to Aberrant and Trinity's assertion that, &quot;no, the future needn't go this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> - The game uses the same base system as Scion, a far more action-oriented version of the Attribute + Ability classic system. You'll see a familiar-looking character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So will &quot;the world as dominated by Cults of Superpowered-Celebrity&quot; setting begin in the not to distant future from the base &quot;now&quot; of the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:42:01-07:00","id":234887,"title":"","content":"Enjoy Neall's post above, because he was kind of not supposed to discuss the underlying metaphysics of the universe. I see it alleviated some concerns about where we're going, so I'll let it stay for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234256#post234256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just plain fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's our ultimate aim on this.<br /> <br /> While roleplaying is a kind of game (and thus about having fun), storygames in the WW/OP milieu typically trend darker, with a lot of implicit questions about meaning and philosophy. While we're certainly not saying there isn't any deeper material here (believe me, there's plenty), the Trinity Continuum is ultimately a game where you can just beat the snot out of Nazi robots from the inner Earth. We're totally fine if that's what you want to do, because that shit is <i>fun</i>, and it's exactly the sort of thing our setting supports. So why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So will &quot;the world as dominated by Cults of Superpowered-Celebrity&quot; setting begin in the not to distant future from the base &quot;now&quot; of the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still subject to change, but the Aberrant setting is planned on being around 2028. If that rough date sounds familiar: yes, it's intentional. Begin speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:31:37-07:00","id":234927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234887#post234887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still subject to change, but the Aberrant setting is planned on being around 2028. If that rough date sounds familiar: yes, it's intentional. Begin speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that means you're pushing the timeline back rather than making the Aberrant War the default setting. While I think a lot of Aberrant needs setting clean-up, the core thematic elements of a world that worships Novas and the capitalist, religious, and political outgrowths of that was what interested me in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T19:46:17-07:00","id":234934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234927#post234927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that means you're pushing the timeline back rather than making the Aberrant War the default setting. While I think a lot of Aberrant needs setting clean-up, the core thematic elements of a world that worships Novas and the capitalist, religious, and political outgrowths of that was what interested me in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aberrant War originally began in 2054. Even going by the original timeline, we'd have more than 20 years to go before that point.<br /> <br /> Also see the earlier discussion about fated futures (or lack thereof) earlier in the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:01:44-07:00","id":234943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kumarei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=233196#post233196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A Caribbean/Central American group (leaving them unnamed because their name is changing before release). This is a group of freedom fighters whose goal is to take down dictatorships across the world. I really liked this group a lot. They were depicted in a very positive light, and it was pretty clear that although their methods were morally ambiguous, their goals were good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any hint on whether their goals are more &quot;classical liberal&quot; or &quot;anarcho-socialist&quot;? To put it in genre-nerd terms: V for Vendetta the movie, or V for Vendetta the graphic novel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:04:58-07:00","id":234944,"title":"","content":"Does that mean that the Trinity Continuum is going to be more of a network of timelines rather than a single timeline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:06:48-07:00","id":234947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234934#post234934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Aberrant War originally began in 2054. Even going by the original timeline, we'd have more than 20 years to go before that point.<br /> <br /> Also see the earlier discussion about fated futures (or lack thereof) earlier in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OH! Right, sorry - and I just placed the 2028 reference. It's the calculated point of no return year when we'll have pumped so much carbon into the atmosphere (based on current rates of the consumption) that a 2 degree Celsius increase to the global climate will be unavoidable - effectively dooming civilization as we know it.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also one year before Apophis gives is a close shave - so possible double Apocalypse for Nova's to save the world from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-19-2014, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:42:42-07:00","id":234980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234944#post234944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean that the Trinity Continuum is going to be more of a network of timelines rather than a single timeline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately &quot;yes&quot; and &quot;no&quot; are both equally true answers to this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:59:00-07:00","id":234991,"title":"","content":"The only way I can see for that to be so is if all of the official settings in the Continuum to be at different points of a single timeline, but for the books to encourage the Storyteller (you\u2019re still calling him that, right?) to diverge from it. <br /> <br /> I won\u2019t ask any further, since you\u2019ve stated a desire to keep the Continuum\u2019s metaphysics under wraps for a little while longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T21:03:57-07:00","id":235004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234991#post234991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller (you\u2019re still calling him that, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We&quot; are in the sense that we're using it as a shorthand during production, since we're all used to talking about Storytellers.<br /> <br /> However, this is not the Storyteller (or Storytelling) system, so that term will not appear in the final product except in the lower-case-s sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T23:38:09-07:00","id":235115,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d urge you to keep it. Sure, it\u2019s not the Storytell(er/ing) System; but it\u2019s still a storytelling system. Unless, you know, you\u2019re going with something like the Narrator of the Narrative System. Just, please, don\u2019t go with \u201cgame master\u201d. (As an aside, I wish Fate Core had gone with Storyteller or Narrator rather than GM.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T02:35:43-07:00","id":235223,"title":"","content":"Isn't 2028 when the next y2k type of calendering bug is due?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T06:36:06-07:00","id":235349,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like the &quot;Continuum&quot; and &quot;Fringe&quot; influences. I've found &quot;Continuum&quot; to be intolerably boring and &quot;Fringe&quot; stopped being worth watching half way through Season 3. <br /> <br /> Ian, is there still an &quot;Adventure! Tales of the Aeon Society&quot; RPG set in the Pulp Era in &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;? &quot;Adventure!&quot; was my favorite - the one that felt most like Warren Ellis' Planetary. <br /> <br /> Mega-Attributes really shouldn't be time and space dependent. A Character who's super-intelligent in the modern day shouldn't suddenly become Kim Kardashian in 1933. That would break the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3736-drprimoris","name":"DrPrimoris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T08:33:31-07:00","id":235432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrPrimoris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=235349#post235349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ian, is there still an &quot;Adventure! Tales of the Aeon Society&quot; RPG set in the Pulp Era in &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;? &quot;Adventure!&quot; was my favorite - the one that felt most like Warren Ellis' Planetary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup - here you go: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/games/tc/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/games/tc/</a> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T08:54:03-07:00","id":235440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=235115#post235115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d urge you to keep it. Sure, it\u2019s not the Storytell(er/ing) System; but it\u2019s still a storytelling system. Unless, you know, you\u2019re going with something like the Narrator of the Narrative System. Just, please, don\u2019t go with \u201cgame master\u201d. (As an aside, I wish Fate Core had gone with Storyteller or Narrator rather than GM.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not interested in potentially endangering our license with CCP at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:19:27-07:00","id":235535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=234707#post234707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't quite decided on that yet. Things like Intelligence are still rated Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to state I'm not looking to start a fight, just understand the design principals.<br /> <br /> I would be happy for an answer from any of the devs, but especially Neall or Ian (Neall seems like a nice guy, and I've known Ian digitally for practically since Aberrant came out). So, if you haven't decided how to approach executing Mega-Attributes in some other way, why decide to take them out completely before coming up with a viable alternative? Are they sen as that problematic that they just have to go? How would you keep intact the granularity and flexibility of the old method? I'm very curious. I understand you can't talk specifics, but I knoa many people who still play the game that they base their builds more off their Mega-Atts than &quot;kewl powers.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3108-malckuss","name":"Malckuss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:28:43-07:00","id":235549,"title":"","content":"I am very sorry I got the ball rolling on bombarding the writers with worries about Mega-Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:44:03-07:00","id":235569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malckuss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=235535#post235535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to state I'm not looking to start a fight, just understand the design principals.<br /> <br /> I would be happy for an answer from any of the devs, but especially Neall or Ian (Neall seems like a nice guy, and I've known Ian digitally for practically since Aberrant came out). So, if you haven't decided how to approach executing Mega-Attributes in some other way, why decide to take them out completely before coming up with a viable alternative? Are they sen as that problematic that they just have to go? How would you keep intact the granularity and flexibility of the old method? I'm very curious. I understand you can't talk specifics, but I knoa many people who still play the game that they base their builds more off their Mega-Atts than &quot;kewl powers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lemme give you a story.<br /> <br /> Let's say you have a house built out of stone. It's not a bad house -- it provides shelter from the elements -- but it could stand to use a lot of improvements. Temperature regulation, electricity run up to code, functional plumbing, all that. So you decide to build a new one.<br /> <br /> As you're building the new house, a neighbour asks &quot;what are you doing for your fireplace?&quot; You shrug. &quot;I don't know. Maybe do it properly out of brick. Maybe a gas fireplace or one of those built-in fake fireplace heaters, which we can tie into the heating system. Maybe with the heating system we won't need a fireplace at all. There are a lot of options we're looking at. We're still nailing down specifics while we're building the structure. We have plenty of time to decide before we figure out the pieces we need to incorporate it into the rest of the structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> The neighbour frowns. &quot;If you don't know what you're replacing it with, why would you get rid of the stone fireplace you have?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 08-20-2014, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T15:50:44-07:00","id":235809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/232420-gencon-panel?p=235440#post235440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're not interested in potentially endangering our license with CCP at this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry; I didn\u2019t realize that calling someone the \u201cstoryteller\u201d would endanger the license. Maybe something like \u201cNarrator\u201d, then? In some ways, that\u2019s potentially even more fitting: when you think about it, <i>everyone</i> in the gaming group is a storyteller; but in the stage plays et al where we get terms such as \u201cscene\u201d as a unit of time, the Narrator is the person who tells the audience what\u2019s going on beyond the actions of the actors on the stage. <br /> <br /> My comment about Fate Core was to illustrate a broader point: IMHO, \u201cgame master\u201d carries implications about the nature of the RPG that narrative-based RPGs are better off without; terms such as \u201cstoryteller\u201d and \u201cnarrator\u201d have different connotations that are much more in keeping with games designed to emphasize story and character over treating it as a strategy game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:44:57-07:00","id":235899,"title":"","content":"I think GM has been established for many years as the main adjudicator of rules. I say &quot;main&quot; simply because the party has say in things. The GM title has also been used in so many games that any connotation (negative or positive) is just something that individuals apply to it.<br /> I say this while wearing a shirt an ex-girlfriend got me that says &quot;You're not the DM of me.&quot; BTW. I cut my teeth with 1st edition D&amp;D so, in my heart, the title has always been DM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}